# ───────── CoBrA / cecon .gitignore ─────────
# Build & distribution artifacts
build/
# build-wip and any sibling build tree, at ANY depth — 1,145 files of it were
# TRACKED until 2026-09-01. (Inline comments are NOT gitignore syntax; the first
# version of these two patterns carried one and matched nothing.)
build-*/
**/build-*/
dist/
/bin/          # engine binaries are git-external in the private coordination tree's releases/ (release standard, from 0.14.0)
*.plugin
*.o
*.a
*.dylib
*.so
*.dSYM/

# OS / editor / scratch logs
.DS_Store
*.log
*.tmp
*.Rhistory
.claude/
# The project-scope Claude Code settings ARE law (deny list + PreToolUse guard,
# GATES.md "Mechanical enforcement" 2026-09-02) and travel with the repo; local/ stays private.
!.claude/
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
/CLAUDE.md


# ───────── Python artifacts
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.venv-gate/

# ───────── DATA — NEVER commit datasets (privacy: KOWEPS / Wind / any research data) ─────────
# Binary / columnar data anywhere in the tree
*.hbin
*.dta
*.parquet
*.sav
*.arrow
*.feather
*.pkl
*.npy
# CSV: ignore ALL by default; allow ONLY the public eval goldens we author under tests/eval/golden/
*.csv
!tests/eval/golden/*.csv
# ...including the wave subdirectories. `!tests/eval/golden/*.csv` matches one
# level only, so an oracle that writes its renders into a per-wave folder (the
# aer_b4/tables and aer_w1/w1b_tables shape) had its .csv silently dropped
# while its .txt siblings landed -- and a table writer picks its format FROM
# the extension, so the missing file is exactly the csv-mode pin. Same class as
# the lane-symlink fix above: the intent was always "goldens we author under
# tests/eval/golden/", and the pattern just could not spell a subdirectory.
!tests/eval/golden/**/*.csv
# GA sweep 2026-08-22 (leg ⑤, clonable build). The blanket `*.csv` above is a
# PRIVACY rule — never commit datasets — and it was also swallowing the unit
# tests' own ORACLE files. Measured on a clean clone with no coordination tree above it:
# both binaries built, but ctest failed 80 of 92 with bare FileNotFoundErrors on
# `tests/validate/*_golden.csv`. The tests were not broken; their answers had
# never been committed, so a stranger who cloned this repo could verify 13% of it.
# Whitelisted here because a golden IS the test — it is authored output, not data.
# The one exception is deliberate and named below.
!tests/validate/*_golden.csv
# tsma_golden.csv is 39 MB — 99.7% of all golden bytes, against <100 KB for the
# other forty combined. It stays ignored rather than quietly pushing a 39 MB blob
# into every future clone; the tsma test therefore still needs a provisioned
# fixture, which is a named gap, not a silent one.
tests/validate/tsma_golden.csv
!piet/packaging/sample/fatalities.csv
# BUGLOG probe fixtures: tiny, hand-written, read by name
!**/buglog_probes/BUG-*.csv
# ...and their RUN OUTPUTS, which are not fixtures. `tools/buglog_probes.py` runs each
# probe with cwd = that directory (`subprocess.run(..., cwd=PROBES)`), so a probe that
# writes a file — the only way to assert on a table WRITER's bytes — drops it there on
# every run. Two of those (bug486.txt, bug487.txt) were committed on 2026-09-14 by a
# `git add -A` taken right after a probe run, which makes the tree DIRTY after every
# `probes` leg — and a dirty tree is precisely what merge_gate.sh refuses before it will
# gate anything. Outputs are ignored; an INPUT fixture keeps landing under the same
# `BUG-*` spelling the CSV rule uses.
**/buglog_probes/*.txt
**/buglog_probes/*.tex
!**/buglog_probes/BUG-*.txt
!**/buglog_probes/BUG-*.tex
# (BUG-464's probe used to leave a .stbcal here, which this file used to ignore.
# The probe now erases it BEFORE the assert that stops it, so there is nothing
# to ignore -- and no rule sitting here to hide the NEXT probe's residue.)
# hbin: synthetic panel datasets for golden validation are tracked exceptions
!tests/validate/panel_synth.hbin
!tests/validate/csdid_cluster_synth.hbin
# dta: MI-216 — in-leg drdid 2x2 fixture, a v118 (pandas round-trip, bit-identical)
# conversion of the public/synthetic drdid2x2 doubly-robust-DiD example dataset (id/t/Y/x1/x2/treat,
# 600 rows) so piet_d2d3's d3h case can load it (engine's dta reader rejects the original's legacy
# v114 format); no research/privacy data. See tests/eval/piet_d2d3/README.md item 4.
!tests/eval/piet_d2d3/drdid2x2_v118.dta
# csdid-cluster golden provenance: StataBE truth dumps (regenerable from csdid_cluster_golden.do)
!tests/validate/csdid_cluster_synth_TRUTH.csv
!tests/validate/csdid_cluster_synth_TRUTH_V.csv
!tests/validate/csdid_cluster_synth_SIMPLE.csv
.audit-2026-06-22/

# WebView2 Evergreen bootstrapper — Microsoft's binary, downloaded at package time (piet_setup.iss), never vendored
piet/packaging/MicrosoftEdgeWebview2Setup.exe
dist/
piet/packaging/Output/
piet/packaging/MicrosoftEdgeWebview2Setup.exe

# pangram run artifacts written to the repo root by graph export / postfile.
# Run evidence, regenerated on every pangram run — never source.
pg_fig.svg
pg_s19_named.svg
pg_post
pg_scratch_dir/
build-prof/

# node test deps — never a repo artifact (2026-09-09: a `git add -A` committed this tree once).
# No trailing slash: in every lane worktree this path is a SYMLINK to the main checkout's
# tree, and a directory-only pattern does not match a symlink — `git status` in wt/piet-2
# listed it as untracked until 2026-09-10.
piet/frontend/test/node_modules

# GEO-IO capture (X1, harvested 2026-09-14 from codex/geo-io @0f5a350c). Only
# the two lines that change behaviour are kept: `*.log` (line 20) would swallow
# the round-trip probe's OWN committed log, and the two dot-directories are
# Stata-minted scratch from the falsification run. The branch also carried six
# `!…/{fixture,point}.{shp,shx,dbf}` negations; measured with `git check-ignore`,
# every one of those paths is NOT-IGNORED to begin with, so they overrode
# nothing and are dropped rather than committed as decoration.
!**/aer/geo/stata_roundtrip_check.log
**/aer/geo/.oracle/
**/aer/geo/.roundtrip/
